.TH TRICKLE 1 "October 2026" "ntrickle 2.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
trickle \- application-independent cooperative bandwidth limiter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B trickle
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.B \-\-
.I COMMAND
[\fIARGUMENTS\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B trickle
runs a command with a cooperative bandwidth limit enforced through an
LD_PRELOAD library.  It works with dynamically linked programs that use the
standard libc socket interfaces.
.PP
The installed command is
.BR trickle ;
.B ntrickle
is an optional alias for the same modern implementation.
.PP
The command and all of its arguments must follow
.BR \-\- .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-m, \-\-mode \fIMODE\fR
Select
.BR standalone ,
.BR daemon ,
or
.BR daemon-required .
The default is
.BR daemon ,
which falls back to standalone when the daemon is unreachable.
.TP
.B \-d, \-\-download \fIRATE\fR
Set the maximum download rate.  A unit is required, for example
.BR 10M ,
.BR 500K ,
.BR 100Mbps ,
.BR 100B ,
or
.BR unlimited .
.TP
.B \-u, \-\-upload \fIRATE\fR
Set the maximum upload rate, using the same syntax as
.BR \-d .
.TP
.B \-w, \-\-window \fIKB\fR
Set the peak-detection window in kilobytes.  The default is 200.
.TP
.B \-W, \-\-weight \fIN\fR
Set the bandwidth share weight.  The minimum is 1.
.TP
.B \-t, \-\-time-smooth \fISECONDS\fR
Set the smoothing time.  The default is 3.0.
.TP
.B \-l, \-\-length-smooth \fIKB\fR
Set the fallback smoothing length.  The default is 20.
.TP
.B \-n, \-\-socket \fIPATH\fR
Use the daemon socket at
.IR PATH .
.TP
.B \-\-schedules \fIPATH\fR
Use the specified
.B schedules.toml
file.
.TP
.B \-\-process-config \fIPATH\fR
Use the specified
.B process.toml
file.
.TP
.B \-\-suppress-warnings
Suppress schedule-collision warnings.
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Print help and exit.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B trickle top [\-\-once] [\-\-interval \fISECONDS\fR] [\-\-socket \fIPATH\fR]
Interactive ncurses dashboard.  The TUI reads the daemon control socket.
.TP
.B trickle stats
Print a snapshot of daemon limits, users, and sessions.
.TP
.B trickle config validate
Validate the daemon, process, and schedule configuration files.
.TP
.B trickle doctor
Run diagnostic checks for the preload library, sockets, and configuration.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.B trickle
sets
.BR NTRICKLE_*
variables for the preload library and the wrapped process.  These are an
internal interface; use the command-line options instead of setting them
directly.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/ntrickle/process.toml
Per-process weight and limit overrides.
.TP
.I /etc/ntrickle/schedules.toml
Time-based limit overrides.
.TP
.I /etc/ntrickle/ntrickled.toml
Daemon configuration.
.SH COMPATIBILITY
This is the modern ntrickle command-line interface.  Classic trickle
compatibility is deliberately not provided: classic
.B \-s
standalone, bare KB/s rates, inline rate schedules,
.BR /etc/trickled.conf ,
.BR TRICKLE_* ,
.BR trickle-overload.so ,
and the classic daemon protocol are not supported.  Classic invocations that
would otherwise be silently misinterpreted are rejected with guidance.
See
.I docs/compatibility.md
and
.I docs/migration-classic.md
in the source distribution.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR trickled (8)
